<article class="env-lemma" id="02O0">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02O0">Lemma <span data-tag="02O0">26.11.8</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a scheme whose underlying topological space is a finite discrete set. Then $X$ is affine. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Say $X = \{ x_1, \ldots , x_ n\} $. Then $U_ i = \{ x_ i\} $ is an open neighbourhood of $x_ i$. By Lemma <a href="/tag/01IT" data-tag="01IT">26.11.2</a> it is affine. Hence $X$ is a finite disjoint union of affine schemes, and hence is affine by Lemma <a href="/tag/01I5" data-tag="01I5">26.6.8</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>